{"author":{"id":"7c5527b9befade3b1be0c1d677ac996815288d8332f34269730a5b81425ee5be"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791272046,"nonce":"4Y1iWXrpkzTNx8EIDa2dLaPn3qw=","metadata":{"github-url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/43","origin":"github","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"I_kwDOULtcMc8AAAABVTihfg","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:labels":"","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:number":"43","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:status":"open","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"7bd76b7cad49bce7db0b46b634e3b6e0f4ad3c565b12d28158dc4fb6e48f0581","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:title":"[BUG](Saving) Users can lose their assessment when saving, exporting or after an update","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/43"},"title":"[BUG](Saving) Users can lose their assessment when saving, exporting or after an update","message":"## What users experience\n- **One wrong value blocks saving everything.** A user fills in a long assessment, types one invalid value (for example a negative quantity) and clicks **Save**. The whole save fails, not just that field. If they close the tab, everything since their last successful save is lost.\n- **Export can silently do nothing.** With an invalid value in the draft, **Export** produces no file and no message.\n- **An app update can erase a saved draft.** When we change the saved format (which #41 needs), returning users find the app **empty**, with no explanation, and their next Save overwrites the old draft for good. Older exported files are refused with a generic \"import failed\".\n- **The footer can claim the work is saved when it isn't.** It says \"Draft saved in this browser\" even when nothing has ever been saved, and nothing warns about unsaved changes before closing the tab.\n\n## Why it matters\nLosing hours of input is the worst thing this tool can do to a user. It also blocks other work: any change to the saved format (#41) would currently wipe everyone's drafts.\n\n## What we propose\nRefactor first, then change behaviour:\n1. **Refactor, no visible change:** move all save, load, import and export logic out of the store into one small, tested module.\n2. **Saving never fails because of one field:** the draft is always saved as typed. Validation only decides whether results can be calculated. *(Decision 1)*\n3. **Old drafts are upgraded automatically:** every draft and export file carries a format version, and older versions are upgraded on load. An unknown version shows a clear message and the stored draft is left untouched.\n4. **Export always gives an answer:** it produces a file or shows an error.\n5. **Honest save status:** the footer shows \"Not saved yet\", \"Unsaved changes\" or \"Saved 2 min ago\", or we switch to autosave as proposed in #33. *(Decision 2)*\n\n## Decisions needed\n1. May a draft be saved while some values are invalid? Recommended: **yes**, because validation is for results, not for saving.\n2. Autosave (#33), or keep the Save button and add an unsaved-changes warning?\n3. A file from a *newer* unknown version: refuse it with a clear message (recommended), or try to load what we can?\n\n## Done when\n- [ ] An invalid value never prevents saving or exporting.\n- [ ] A draft saved in today's format opens correctly after the format changes (tested with a saved example file).\n- [ ] An unknown version shows a clear message, and the stored draft is not overwritten.\n- [ ] The footer never says the work is saved when it isn't.\n\n## Technical notes\n- `saveToStorage` (`frontend/src/stores/mitsi.ts`) validates the whole state with `MitsiStateDraftSchema` and returns `false` if any field is invalid.\n- `exportJson` calls `MitsiStateDraftSchema.parse`, which throws a `ZodError`; `exportAssessment` in `MainLayout.vue` doesn't catch it.\n- `parseState` returns `null` for any `schemaVersion` other than `MITSI_SCHEMA_VERSION` (4), and `loadFromStorage` ignores `null` without telling the user.\n- The footer text `mainFooterDraftSaved` is shown whenever `savedAt` is `null`.\n- All four behaviours were confirmed on `dev` at `b35fc8c` with a throwaway store test.\n- Related: #33 (autosave), #41 (blocked by this), #9 (export/import).","files":null}]}